 "text": "Hi, how are you holding up? Try frame it as a together opportunity. Say you'd love her help with tidying up and she can teach you new ways to keep things. Then only she knows about it. Keep the house fun and open. She won't know what to single you for anyway. A busy desk won't give much away. Try saying you' like it tidy and busy, and she can help with the easy bits she knows where they go. Lots of people do. Then only switch it back after she leaves. She'll forget it's even an argument worth winning. And always ask her first before getting rid of something she's already put away. That way it doesn't look like resistance.",
